    <cap:headline>Fishermen warning</cap:headline>
    <cap:description>Gale Wind (speed reaching 70-80 kmph gusting to 90 kmph) very likely over Eastcentral Arabian sea and adjoining Southeast Arabian Sea and Lakshadweep area from 15th May morning. Squally Wind (speed reaching 50-60 kmph gusting to 70 kmph) very likely along and off Kerala-Karnataka coast and speed reaching 40-50 kmph over Gulf of Mannar. Sea
conditions will be high to very high over Eastcentral Arabian Sea; very rough to high over Eastcentral Arabian Sea along and off Karnataka coast and Maharashtra-Goa coast and rough to very rough over Comorin area and along and off Kerala coast; adjoining Lakshadweep-Maldives area and Equatorial Indian Ocean. Tidal wave Warning: Tidal wave of about 1 meter height above the astronomical tide is very likely to inundate low lying areas of Lakshadweep Islands. Fishermen are advised not to venture into these areas.</cap:description>
    <cap:instruction>Action suggested:
• Deep sea fishermen are advised to return to coasts by 14th May.</cap:instruction>
    <cap:web>http://www.rsmcnewdelhi.imd.gov.in</cap:web>
